---
title: "Theme Builder Import and Export"
---

{% warning %}
This is AI generated and not reviewed, don't read it yet :)
{% /warning %}

The [Theme Builder](/theme-builder/) provides a visual interface for creating and customising AG Grid themes. You can export themes to use in your application, and import existing theme code back into the Theme Builder for further modifications.

## Exporting Themes

To export your theme from Theme Builder:

1. Click the **Import / Export** button at the bottom left of the Theme Builder
2. The **Export** tab shows JavaScript code that creates your theme
3. Click **Download** to save as a file, or **Copy** to copy to your clipboard

The exported code defines a theme using [Theme Parts](./theming-parts/) and [Theme Parameters](./theming-parameters/):

```js
import { themeQuartz, iconSetQuartzLight } from 'ag-grid-community';

export const myTheme = themeQuartz
    .withPart(iconSetQuartzLight)
    .withParams({
        accentColor: "#5A9F7D",
        borderRadius: 8,
        headerTextColor: "#2E4A3F"
    });
```

To use the exported theme, save the code to a file and pass the theme to the `theme` grid option. See [Built-in Themes](./themes/) for framework-specific examples of applying themes.

## Importing Themes

Theme Builder can import existing theme code, allowing you to make visual adjustments to a theme that was previously exported or hand-written.

To import a theme:

1. Click the **Import / Export** button in the Theme Builder toolbar
2. Select the **Import** tab
3. Either:
   - Paste your theme code into the text area, or
   - Click **Upload** to select a `.js` or `.ts` file, or
   - Drag and drop a file onto the dialog

4. Click **Apply** to import the theme

### Import Limitations

Not all theme code can be imported into Theme Builder. The import feature is designed to work with code that was exported from Theme Builder, and has the following limitations:

- **Only recognised parameters are imported** - Theme Builder supports a subset of all available [Theme Parameters](./theming-parameters/). Unrecognised parameters are ignored. You will see a warning listing any ignored parameters.

- **Values must be literals** - Parameter values must be literal values such as strings, numbers, or objects. JavaScript variables or expressions (e.g. `accentColor: brandColor` or `spacing: baseSpacing * 2`) cannot be evaluated and will be ignored.

- **Theme parts are recognised** - Built-in theme parts like `iconSetQuartzLight` or `colorSchemeLight` are recognised and applied. Custom parts are not supported.

- **Comments are ignored** - JavaScript comments in your code are parsed and ignored.

- **Only withParams() content is imported** - Any custom CSS, additional exports, or code outside of the theme definition is not imported.

If your code contains features that cannot be imported, Theme Builder will display warnings explaining what was ignored. The imported theme will include all compatible settings.

